# counter scope 100 — take the WebSocket connection.
#
# The chassis stamps `@websocket.upgrade = true` on any request that asks
# to upgrade, whatever its path, and does nothing else on its own. WHICH
# paths become sessions, and for whom, is this stack's decision: this op
# is where a session cookie check, an Origin allowlist, or a subprotocol
# would go (`WITH origins = &array("app.example"), subprotocols = …`).
#
# `events = &array("close")` opts into one extra run when the session
# ends (see _websocket/900/closed.txcl). Every later message runs at
# counter/_websocket/0 — the stack nested under this one, like _mail.
WHEN @websocket.upgrade == true && @web.req.url.path == "/ws"
  EXEC "txco://websocket/accept"
  WITH events = &array("close")
